{"type":"message","id":"6199f217","parentId":"21df871f","timestamp":"2026-03-24T05:56:37.173Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering reviews and comments**\n\nI think I need to check for reviews or comments. I can use a command like `gh pr view` along with the options for reviews and comments. It seems like a straightforward way to gather the feedback I’m looking for. By using this, I’ll be able to get a better understanding of what people think and any necessary adjustments that might be needed. Let's try that out efficiently!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_050a45ec585c4d650169c2279263b881919242ebc15d972342\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpwieUBvCUDnbTmUjXDu0BQNBaTykC9xWeojDx80h0Uawhzy1TrDP3Nm9XbKNZJq5j-MIlYnQqw-z7aNv6DXlJLRYDe-PcAbZjqe6OGDr67pzL2CrgIUxbMdJ3znfcRwtG49yVR3nAfp4T3Aq9O6493m5xdPoXA-iV7mI9XBAbHMhg4N7obYAzpFPaCg08GYEdaIq9BAY7YjreNAf0xY8keRt_huqGmypZkhyQRn6ivismikpd_TvuMbnyVVgDw4Nq5WeR5wtwNTxgLTUiDRCTIOAhLUqf11hq4RYZjxDSZw9jfA8CFDWFcgoGCNfgiXnyFKHF1TiOghvQzJftYUnxh9Hz2sR8mSnpZzNO1vjZ-1aUQnCTANjZT_iuy768TQYUIdhjFF_SYZloBQaQy1PQq0S6QLshj55ONpZhEFtPTM8u6zRwHj55EGCfSJ8mvCovzQ37aSp7w5Vm9HHLlW6biJIr8F5MwExbN_gUiy9OGZ8ORBzPoB2sdr3IHDn9QB1qkIaN7Q3L-Ciltnlly9I_ky2goyd3fSKOwtfNF4W8TW_C38cTnzSfWlqgcYwAl3sk_WW1OPMSzwRpUBaZ0m_dk03sncj48w17JARQPPA3u4zUEiN9dqFC20e-uJfqcm6k_zkJiAIAU68XhHwsmr4n2ZX0WW6FQ1iPCtWyU8ChnkrXa0Wv7otNK8tjOBJMq2qpPxLkUaTPQKy2R94f34vp6pOMoop70rLwwUXBXznpL_sHs1Mi7fGA2y5un-rk-aRHPOKEx8PEKS-wdbuRRqTmyJjWWfMPGFdDp3_Z15fC6BRgHUbXBkJbtvRxqStRZRuzT6qV2UD9e1mx22xajBrHweUmGx8jceKtSC4KcLnd7uPcFqQY4nrH6W9nwfqhv9bMGb-fx3-4MuUYIuIeGQ8bhIZa5g==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering reviews and comments**\\n\\nI think I need to check for reviews or comments. I can use a command like `gh pr view` along with the options for reviews and comments. It seems like a straightforward way to gather the feedback I’m looking for. By using this, I’ll be able to get a better understanding of what people think and any necessary adjustments that might be needed. Let's try that out efficiently!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_rBougEigjcYKPjEqsSYd2tkM|fc_050a45ec585c4d650169c22794da588191ab747807f506fbe3","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh pr view 52597 --repo openclaw/openclaw --comments --json number,title,state,reviewDecision,comments,reviews,latestReviews,body,url","workdir":"/root/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":30},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"gh pr view 52597 --repo openclaw/openclaw --comments --json number,title,state,reviewDecision,comments,reviews,latestReviews,body,url\",\"workdir\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000,\"timeout\":30}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":4291,"output":91,"cacheRead":30592,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34974,"cost":{"input":0.010727500000000001,"output":0.0013650000000000001,"cacheRead":0.007647999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0197405}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774331793442}}
{"type":"message","id":"38bf90c1","parentId":"6199f217","timestamp":"2026-03-24T05:56:38.023Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_rBougEigjcYKPjEqsSYd2tkM|fc_050a45ec585c4d650169c22794da588191ab747807f506fbe3","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"body\":\"## Summary\\nFixes Feishu extension tool duplication by removing the extra static `skills` registration from the plugin manifest.\\n\\nCloses #52572.\\n\\n## Cause\\nThe Feishu extension registered skills in two places:\\n- `extensions/feishu/openclaw.plugin.json` via `\\\"skills\\\": [\\\"./skills\\\"]`\\n- `extensions/feishu/index.ts` inside `registerFull()`\\n\\nThat caused Feishu tools to be registered twice.\\n\\n## Changes\\n- remove the `skills` entry from `extensions/feishu/openclaw.plugin.json`\\n- update generated bundled plugin metadata to match the manifest change\\n\\n`registerFull()` remains intact, so runtime/channel initialization and Feishu-specific setup are unchanged.\\n\\n## Testing\\n- `pnpm test:extension feishu`\\n  - Result: 49 test files passed, 472 tests passed\\n\\n## Notes\\n- I used `--no-verify` for the local commit because this machine's runtime config (`/root/.openclaw/openclaw.json`) makes unrelated repo-wide pre-commit checks fail locally.\\n- The actual Feishu extension test suite passed after the change.\\n\\n## AI usage\\nAI-assisted\\n\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOQb6kR8701sGO\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"greptile-apps\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"body\":\"<h3>Greptile Summary</h3>\\n\\nThis PR fixes a double skill registration bug in the Feishu extension by removing the static `\\\"skills\\\": [\\\"./skills\\\"]` entry from `extensions/feishu/openclaw.plugin.json` (and the corresponding generated metadata file). All Feishu tools are already registered programmatically through `registerFull()` in `index.ts`, making the static `skills` path redundant.\\n\\n- Removes `\\\"skills\\\": [\\\"./skills\\\"]` from the Feishu plugin manifest — the `skills/` directory contains only `SKILL.md` documentation files, not code, and `registerFull()` is the single source of truth for tool registration.\\n- Updates `bundled-plugin-metadata.generated.ts` to stay in sync with the manifest change.\\n- `registerFull()` and all channel/runtime setup in `index.ts` are untouched, so functionality is fully preserved.\\n- 472 tests passed after the change per the author.\\n\\n<h3>Confidence Score: 5/5</h3>\\n\\n- Safe to merge — the change is a minimal, targeted removal of a duplicate registration entry with no functional side effects.\\n- The fix is a two-line removal that addresses a clearly identified root cause. `registerFull()` remains the sole authoritative registration path, the `skills/` directory only held documentation (`SKILL.md`) files rather than code, and the generated file is correctly kept in sync. The full test suite (472 tests) passed after the change.\\n- No files require special attention.\\n\\n<!-- greptile_other_comments_section -->\\n\\n<sub>Reviews (1): Last reviewed commit: [\\\"fix(feishu): avoid double skill registra...\\\"](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/commit/c002c6c21a5f1d036e3dcfd986b3254f1a44f363) | [Re-trigger Greptile](https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=25999570)</sub>\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:13:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/52597#issuecomment-4107714958\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOQb6kR87025pi\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"zslun168\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"I fixed this locally in commit `683b8c2` by removing `skills: [\\\"./skills\\\"]` from `extensions/feishu/openclaw.plugin.json`.\\\\n\\\\nThat avoids duplicate registration of the Feishu skills, since they are already registered in `registerFull()`.\\\\n\\\\nIf you'd like, you can cherry-pick it with:\\\\n`git cherry-pick 683b8c2`\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-03-23T05:05:37Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/52597#issuecomment-4108032610\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false}],\"latestReviews\":[{\"id\":\"\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `c002c6c21a`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\nCodex has been enabled to automatically review pull requests in this repo. Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nWhen you [sign up for Codex through ChatGPT](https://openai.com/codex), Codex can also answer questions or update the PR, like \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:14:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"\"}}],\"number\":52597,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOQb6kR87txNWJ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `c002c6c21a`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\nCodex has been enabled to automatically review pull requests in this repo. Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nWhen you [sign up for Codex through ChatGPT](https://openai.com/codex), Codex can also answer questions or update the PR, like \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:14:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"c002c6c21a5f1d036e3dcfd986b3254f1a44f363\"}}],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"fix(feishu): avoid double skill registration\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/52597\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":840,"aggregated":"{\"body\":\"## Summary\\nFixes Feishu extension tool duplication by removing the extra static `skills` registration from the plugin manifest.\\n\\nCloses #52572.\\n\\n## Cause\\nThe Feishu extension registered skills in two places:\\n- `extensions/feishu/openclaw.plugin.json` via `\\\"skills\\\": [\\\"./skills\\\"]`\\n- `extensions/feishu/index.ts` inside `registerFull()`\\n\\nThat caused Feishu tools to be registered twice.\\n\\n## Changes\\n- remove the `skills` entry from `extensions/feishu/openclaw.plugin.json`\\n- update generated bundled plugin metadata to match the manifest change\\n\\n`registerFull()` remains intact, so runtime/channel initialization and Feishu-specific setup are unchanged.\\n\\n## Testing\\n- `pnpm test:extension feishu`\\n  - Result: 49 test files passed, 472 tests passed\\n\\n## Notes\\n- I used `--no-verify` for the local commit because this machine's runtime config (`/root/.openclaw/openclaw.json`) makes unrelated repo-wide pre-commit checks fail locally.\\n- The actual Feishu extension test suite passed after the change.\\n\\n## AI usage\\nAI-assisted\\n\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOQb6kR8701sGO\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"greptile-apps\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"body\":\"<h3>Greptile Summary</h3>\\n\\nThis PR fixes a double skill registration bug in the Feishu extension by removing the static `\\\"skills\\\": [\\\"./skills\\\"]` entry from `extensions/feishu/openclaw.plugin.json` (and the corresponding generated metadata file). All Feishu tools are already registered programmatically through `registerFull()` in `index.ts`, making the static `skills` path redundant.\\n\\n- Removes `\\\"skills\\\": [\\\"./skills\\\"]` from the Feishu plugin manifest — the `skills/` directory contains only `SKILL.md` documentation files, not code, and `registerFull()` is the single source of truth for tool registration.\\n- Updates `bundled-plugin-metadata.generated.ts` to stay in sync with the manifest change.\\n- `registerFull()` and all channel/runtime setup in `index.ts` are untouched, so functionality is fully preserved.\\n- 472 tests passed after the change per the author.\\n\\n<h3>Confidence Score: 5/5</h3>\\n\\n- Safe to merge — the change is a minimal, targeted removal of a duplicate registration entry with no functional side effects.\\n- The fix is a two-line removal that addresses a clearly identified root cause. `registerFull()` remains the sole authoritative registration path, the `skills/` directory only held documentation (`SKILL.md`) files rather than code, and the generated file is correctly kept in sync. The full test suite (472 tests) passed after the change.\\n- No files require special attention.\\n\\n<!-- greptile_other_comments_section -->\\n\\n<sub>Reviews (1): Last reviewed commit: [\\\"fix(feishu): avoid double skill registra...\\\"](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/commit/c002c6c21a5f1d036e3dcfd986b3254f1a44f363) | [Re-trigger Greptile](https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=25999570)</sub>\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:13:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/52597#issuecomment-4107714958\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOQb6kR87025pi\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"zslun168\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"I fixed this locally in commit `683b8c2` by removing `skills: [\\\"./skills\\\"]` from `extensions/feishu/openclaw.plugin.json`.\\\\n\\\\nThat avoids duplicate registration of the Feishu skills, since they are already registered in `registerFull()`.\\\\n\\\\nIf you'd like, you can cherry-pick it with:\\\\n`git cherry-pick 683b8c2`\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-03-23T05:05:37Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/52597#issuecomment-4108032610\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false}],\"latestReviews\":[{\"id\":\"\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `c002c6c21a`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\nCodex has been enabled to automatically review pull requests in this repo. Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nWhen you [sign up for Codex through ChatGPT](https://openai.com/codex), Codex can also answer questions or update the PR, like \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:14:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"\"}}],\"number\":52597,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOQb6kR87txNWJ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `c002c6c21a`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\nCodex has been enabled to automatically review pull requests in this repo. Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex revie