{"type":"message","id":"a458e849","parentId":"e37cba8c","timestamp":"2026-03-24T13:41:38.960Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_050a45ec585c4d650169c294784af481919ad90734664a87d3\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpwpR5fVmfisbflGDC74DRWZqCwPIwsX4_x8ScIf8BxyBnrWyVejzwSr_gdB3_2PVJt0F4ayP_6E0N5e0y7S4Vyn6gh8LeuknFSm4CLo_0iTPu2u5SDncB5Eenrr_NB3QyWSSGdlRX2G960HmDbaF7OQKFq_WA9dmIrknPO-j6SrNzp3kww2XujHoZIA6wiStca909kgnV22DCypC1JqcH2Hze5Fo_z29XBr894KTanCe00nv2BuFufrPEopL5U9p2HA-lc2Wy5IDcuTjSyZz4F1RJy-fUlmcKXUT_fL5CdaYw8_k8IcqmmftuNq67EkEdwv3aoj60DaaOShiBBvQmCggA6akbZv7KfRAMKpiAe306b1nbugvQ0ZZ7e2oOVxKcxxs19Cp5s9hU0MKpWXtcP_NBsWXcPMA1bcZsB0om0OqUYY_CmosuxL1kPEdXKLDv_yQUVAZKJR47FQKSleMXqGMgRFRPR1jRYGvc6o_PtryhrxhSZ6rnvLB8LmvD-fCKy3X3maAtSgnwoDg3FVRMFm4NcHtDWjvMRB_w_BvYMxEQ0JzbUJR3aHHotcFZZUngo-9N-JR5JAgWudUy8-4KMZIDQ-UK6k4nCB7MuLM0KpjkzBypszI1cS_RIfpBgdCMh1VCD4Iiu42UO7R7aSWPs_5q0DFK7Dh48i2NDd3iIX1ZjKtNdQYgqB9sgjFTw6C3BxmWCXzUW4rVAi5E_RTcsApnldmwh6R0JMlYWQUC1k1B0uW2C2PYinG4lDsz3i45BuPuqasuRdtvivPdMPK_3uFS78B3bhI2Jt5gQDO3JRGfQJ9H8AlLtmyWK3OBiK4Qk3oMHCb3XZn4cptDOQu1IXIARPdDm8RyM-0gvwvkf3rDCF8sDByLlnnlhwt28bl3To2nRujhvls6PzGhH9OPAU24M4MD8s4h099pxBrt_CXF9cnwIp2psjA6Y6CNONWvdxVIOfUOzHWIXJYhYyfHUr-Zj6-w15rA0oR0-mU5NwNapP8=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 好，我直接往下收敛成可提交的问题。\n\n## 这条问题我建议这样定义\n**先按 docs / behavior clarification 提。**  \n不要一上来咬死是 bug，这样更稳，更容易被接。\n\n---\n\n## 建议标题\n### 英文版\n**Group chat routing is unclear when no explicit group-to-agent binding is configured**\n\n### 更偏问题感的版本\n**Feishu group chats can route to an agent even without an explicit group-to-agent binding, but the routing rule is unclear**\n\n我更推荐第一条，干净、专业、不容易被反感。\n\n---\n\n## 建议 issue 描述草稿\n\n### Summary\nIn a multi-agent Feishu setup, a group chat can still route to an agent even when the group chat ID is not explicitly bound to that agent in config.\n\nThe behavior may be intentional, but the routing rule is currently unclear from a user/operator perspective:\n- why this group ends up on a specific agent\n- whether the behavior is stable across restart\n- whether it comes from a default fallback, a session binding, or a last-route mechanism\n- what the recommended config is for deterministic group routing\n\nThis makes multi-agent group setup hard to reason about and easy to misconfigure.\n\n### Why this matters\nFor multi-agent deployments, group-chat routing is a core behavior, not an edge case.\n\nIf a group can reach an agent without an explicit binding, users need a clear explanation of:\n- what rule is being applied\n- whether that rule is persistent\n- when explicit config is required\n- how to avoid accidental or drifting routing\n\nOtherwise, operators may think their config is correct when they are actually relying on implicit behavior.\n\n### Current observed behavior\n- A Feishu group chat is currently reaching an agent successfully\n- The group chat ID was not explicitly bound to that agent in config\n- From the outside, it is not obvious whether this comes from:\n  - default routing to `main`\n  - an existing session route\n  - automatic group session creation\n  - some other fallback rule\n\n### Expected behavior\nOne of the following should be true, and documented clearly:\n\n1. **If implicit routing is intended**\n   - document the exact fallback rule\n   - explain how it behaves across restart\n   - explain how it interacts with multi-agent setups\n\n2. **If explicit binding is required for deterministic routing**\n   - document that clearly\n   - warn users when a group is operating through fallback routing instead of explicit config\n\n### Suggested improvement\nAt minimum, this likely needs a docs clarification covering:\n- how group chats are routed when no explicit group-to-agent binding exists\n- whether `main` is the default fallback\n- whether session history / last-route affects future routing\n- what config is recommended for stable multi-agent group routing\n\nOptionally, the runtime/status output could also expose whether a group is using:\n- explicit binding\n- fallback/default routing\n- remembered session route\n\n### Environment\n- OpenClaw: current multi-agent Feishu deployment\n- Surface: Feishu group chat\n- Scenario: group works, but no explicit group-ID-to-agent binding was configured\n\n---\n\n## 中文版意思\n这条 issue 的核心不是：\n> “没绑也能路由，所以系统错了”\n\n而是：\n> **没显式绑定时，群聊到底为什么会落到某个 agent，这件事对用户不透明。**\n\n这个提法更强，因为它不容易被一句“这是预期行为”打回来。  \n即便维护者说“是预期”，那也 still 说明：\n**文档没讲清。**\n\n---\n\n## 我建议补的证据\n如果你后面真要把它发出去，最好再补 3 个点，issue 会更硬：\n\n### 1. 配置证据\n明确写：\n- 当前配置没有把这个群 ID 显式绑定给某个 agent\n\n### 2. 观察证据\n明确写：\n- 这个群现在实际稳定进入 `main`\n\n### 3. 稳定性验证\n最好再测一下：\n- gateway 重启后是否还是进 `main`\n- 换个新群是不是也一样\n- 是否和 session history / last route 有关系\n\n---\n\n## 我对这条问题的判断\n这条很适合做成：\n\n- **高质量 issue**\n- 或者先做 **docs issue / docs PR**\n\n它的价值在于：\n- 多 Agent 用户一定会踩\n- 不属于小众边角\n- 而且你这里已经有真实场景，不是空想\n\n---\n\n## 下一步我建议\n我继续按这个方向推进的话，优先级这样排：\n\n1. **先把这条 issue 草稿定稿**\n2. **再查当前配置 / 路由证据，补强 issue**\n3. **然后顺手把 docs 修复点一起列出来**\n\n你既然说“继续”，那我下一轮就默认按这个方向往 **可直接提交版本** 收。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_050a45ec585c4d650169c29479dde881918fdeca2d346fb5b4\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":105116,"output":1087,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":106203,"cost":{"input":0.26279,"output":0.016305,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.27909500000000004}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774359668360}}
